                <pb facs="0728" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg648"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Canal.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 543.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your favor dated September 3, 1902, informing me of the action of the late
                    Vice-Admiral Killick in seizing certain goods destined for the Cape on the
                    German steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Markomannia.</hi></p>
                <p>In reply to your communication I have the honor to state to your Excellency that
                    it will receive my earnest attention.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
